{"custom_id": "prompt::70", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef make_tmp_dir(prefix):\n    now = datetime.now().isoformat()\n    f_uuid = uuid.uuid4().hex\n    out_dir = '{out}/{p}-{now}-{uuid}'.format(out=_output_dir, p=prefix, now=now, uuid=f_uuid)\n    if not _dry_run:\n        os.makedirs(out_dir)\n    log.msg_debug('Output directory: {out_dir}'.format(out_dir=_output_dir))\n    return out_dir\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nCreate a temporary directory\n\n    :param prefix(str): Name prefix for the new directory\n    :return: a string with the resulting name of new directory\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nCreate temporary directory with unique name based on current time and UUID. If not in dry run mode, create directory. Log debug message about output directory. Return path of new directory.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "prompt::71", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_cached_token(self):\n    token_info = None\n    if self.cache_path:\n        try:\n            f = open(self.cache_path)\n            token_info_string = f.read()\n            f.close()\n            token_info = json.loads(token_info_string)\n            if self.is_token_expired(token_info):\n                token_info = self.refresh_access_token(token_info['refresh_token'])\n        except IOError:\n            pass\n    return token_info\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nGets a cached auth token\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `get_cached_token` checks if cache path exists. If it does, tries to open and read cached token info. Parses JSON from file content. Checks if token is expired using `is_token_expired`. If expired, refreshes token with `refresh_access_token` using old refresh token. Returns parsed token info or `None` if any errors occur during process.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "prompt::72", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef to_date_field(formatter):\n\n    class DateConverter(object):\n\n        def __init__(self, formatter):\n            self.formatter = formatter\n\n        def __call__(self, value):\n            if isinstance(value, string_types):\n                value = datetime.strptime(value, self.formatter).date()\n            if isinstance(value, datetime):\n                value = value.date()\n            return value\n    return DateConverter(formatter)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReturns a callable instance that will convert a string to a Date.\n\n    :param formatter: String that represents data format for parsing.\n    :return: instance of the DateConverter.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `to_date_field` takes a date format string and returns a converter object. This converter can take a date string or a datetime object and convert it into a date object using the provided format. If input is already a datetime object, it extracts the date part directly. The returned converter object has a call method that performs this conversion.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "prompt::73", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef callgraph(G, stmt_list):\n    func_list = []\n    for stmt in stmt_list:\n        try:\n            G.add_node(stmt.head.ident.name)\n            func_list.append(stmt)\n        except:\n            pass\n    for func in func_list:\n        assert isinstance(func, node.function)\n        func_name = func.head.ident.name\n        for s in node.postorder(func):\n            if s.__class__ is node.funcall and s.func_expr.__class__ is node.ident:\n                G.add_edge(func_name, s.func_expr.name)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nBuild callgraph of func_list, ignoring\n    built-in functions\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `callgraph` takes graph `G` and list of statements `stmt_list`. It adds nodes for functions found in `stmt_list` to graph `G`. Then it iterates over these functions, adding edges to graph `G` for each function call within them. This helps visualize function calls in code structure.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
