{"custom_id": "prompt::160", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_line(self, position):\n    datalen = len(self.data)\n    count = len(self.data[0])\n    line = 1\n    while count < position:\n        if line >= datalen:\n            break\n        count += len(self.data[line]) + 1\n        line += 1\n    return line\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReturns the line number that the given string position is found on\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `get_line` takes `position` as input. It calculates total data length and column count. Starts at first line. Iterates through lines until column count exceeds position. Returns current line number when condition met. If end of data reached without match, returns last line.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
