{"custom_id": "sg_prompt::65", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef filter_publication(publication, cache=_CACHE):\n    if cache is None:\n        cache = load_cache()\n    if publication._get_hash() in cache:\n        return None\n    cache.update([publication._get_hash()])\n    save_cache(cache)\n    return publication\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nDeduplication function, which compares `publication` with samples stored in\n    `cache`. If the match NOT is found, `publication` is returned, else None.\n\n    Args:\n        publication (obj): :class:`.Publication` instance.\n        cache (obj): Cache which is used for lookups.\n\n    Returns:\n        obj/None: Depends whether the object is found in cache or not.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks hash in cache. If found, returns `None`. If not, updates cache and saves it. Returns publication.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "sg_prompt::66", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _parse(self, stream, context, path):\n    objs = []\n    while True:\n        start = stream.tell()\n        test = stream.read(len(self.find))\n        stream.seek(start)\n        if test == self.find:\n            break\n        else:\n            subobj = self.subcon._parse(stream, context, path)\n            objs.append(subobj)\n    return objs\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nParse until a given byte string is found.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nReads data from `stream`. Seeks until finds `self.find`. Parses sub-objects. Collects in `objs`. Returns list of parsed objects.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "sg_prompt::67", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_photometry(self, brightest=False, min_unc=0.02, convert=True):\n    if brightest:\n        row = self.brightest\n    else:\n        row = self.closest\n    if not hasattr(self, 'conversions'):\n        convert = False\n    if convert:\n        bands = self.conversions\n    else:\n        bands = self.bands.keys()\n    d = {}\n    for b in bands:\n        if convert:\n            key = b\n            (mag, dmag) = getattr(self, b)(brightest=brightest)\n        else:\n            key = self.bands[b]\n            (mag, dmag) = (row[b], row['e_{}'.format(b)])\n        d[key] = (mag, max(dmag, min_unc))\n    return d\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReturns dictionary of photometry of closest match\n\n        unless brightest is True, in which case the brightest match.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction fetches photometry data. Checks if brightest star needed. Sets row accordingly. Converts magnitudes if possible. Iterates over bands, fetching magnitudes and uncertainties. Ensures minimum uncertainty applied. Returns dictionary of magnitudes and uncertainties.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
