{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::64", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef parse_devicelist(data_str):\n    p = HTMLTableParser()\n    p.feed(data_str)\n    known_devices = p.tables[9]\n    devices = {}\n    for device in known_devices:\n        if len(device) == 5 and device[2] != '':\n            devices[device[2]] = device[1]\n    return devices\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nParse the BT Home Hub 5 data format.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nHTML table parser feeds data string. Extracts ninth table. Iterates through rows. Checks length five, second column non-empty. Adds to dictionary. Returns dictionary of devices.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::65", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef filter_publication(publication, cache=_CACHE):\n    if cache is None:\n        cache = load_cache()\n    if publication._get_hash() in cache:\n        return None\n    cache.update([publication._get_hash()])\n    save_cache(cache)\n    return publication\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nDeduplication function, which compares `publication` with samples stored in\n    `cache`. If the match NOT is found, `publication` is returned, else None.\n\n    Args:\n        publication (obj): :class:`.Publication` instance.\n        cache (obj): Cache which is used for lookups.\n\n    Returns:\n        obj/None: Depends whether the object is found in cache or not.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks hash in cache. If found, returns none. Updates cache with hash. Saves cache. Returns publication.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::66", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _parse(self, stream, context, path):\n    objs = []\n    while True:\n        start = stream.tell()\n        test = stream.read(len(self.find))\n        stream.seek(start)\n        if test == self.find:\n            break\n        else:\n            subobj = self.subcon._parse(stream, context, path)\n            objs.append(subobj)\n    return objs\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nParse until a given byte string is found.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nReads data from `stream`. Seeks until finds `self.find`. Parses sub-objects. Collects in `objs`. Returns list of parsed objects.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::67", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_photometry(self, brightest=False, min_unc=0.02, convert=True):\n    if brightest:\n        row = self.brightest\n    else:\n        row = self.closest\n    if not hasattr(self, 'conversions'):\n        convert = False\n    if convert:\n        bands = self.conversions\n    else:\n        bands = self.bands.keys()\n    d = {}\n    for b in bands:\n        if convert:\n            key = b\n            (mag, dmag) = getattr(self, b)(brightest=brightest)\n        else:\n            key = self.bands[b]\n            (mag, dmag) = (row[b], row['e_{}'.format(b)])\n        d[key] = (mag, max(dmag, min_unc))\n    return d\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReturns dictionary of photometry of closest match\n\n        unless brightest is True, in which case the brightest match.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction fetches photometry data. Checks if brightest star needed. Sets row accordingly. Converts magnitudes if possible. Iterates over bands, fetching magnitudes and uncertainties. Ensures minimum uncertainty applied. Returns dictionary of magnitudes and uncertainties.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::68", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _get_request_fields_from_parent(self):\n    if not self.parent:\n        return None\n    if not getattr(self.parent, 'request_fields'):\n        return None\n    if not isinstance(self.parent.request_fields, dict):\n        return None\n    return self.parent.request_fields.get(self.field_name)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nGet request fields from the parent serializer.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks parent exists. Parent has request fields? Check type. Get field value. Return it.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::69", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef binaryRecordsStream(self, directory, recordLength=None, process_all=False):\n    deserializer = FileBinaryStreamDeserializer(self._context, recordLength)\n    file_stream = FileStream(directory, process_all)\n    self._on_stop_cb.append(file_stream.stop)\n    return DStream(file_stream, self, deserializer)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nMonitor a directory and process all binary files.\n\n        File names starting with ``.`` are ignored.\n\n        :param string directory: a path\n        :param recordLength: None, int or struct format string\n        :param bool process_all: whether to process pre-existing files\n        :rtype: DStream\n\n        .. warning::\n            Only ``int`` ``recordLength`` are supported in PySpark API.\n            The ``process_all`` parameter does not exist in the PySpark API.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction reads files in directory. Deserializes records. Streams data. Returns stream object.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::70", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef make_tmp_dir(prefix):\n    now = datetime.now().isoformat()\n    f_uuid = uuid.uuid4().hex\n    out_dir = '{out}/{p}-{now}-{uuid}'.format(out=_output_dir, p=prefix, now=now, uuid=f_uuid)\n    if not _dry_run:\n        os.makedirs(out_dir)\n    log.msg_debug('Output directory: {out_dir}'.format(out_dir=_output_dir))\n    return out_dir\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nCreate a temporary directory\n\n    :param prefix(str): Name prefix for the new directory\n    :return: a string with the resulting name of new directory\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nCreate timestamped UUID dir. Check dry run. Make dir. Log debug msg. Return dir path.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::71", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_cached_token(self):\n    token_info = None\n    if self.cache_path:\n        try:\n            f = open(self.cache_path)\n            token_info_string = f.read()\n            f.close()\n            token_info = json.loads(token_info_string)\n            if self.is_token_expired(token_info):\n                token_info = self.refresh_access_token(token_info['refresh_token'])\n        except IOError:\n            pass\n    return token_info\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nGets a cached auth token\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction reads cache file. Checks if path exists. Opens file. Reads content. Closes file. Parses JSON. Checks if expired. Refreshes token if needed. Returns token info.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::72", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef to_date_field(formatter):\n\n    class DateConverter(object):\n\n        def __init__(self, formatter):\n            self.formatter = formatter\n\n        def __call__(self, value):\n            if isinstance(value, string_types):\n                value = datetime.strptime(value, self.formatter).date()\n            if isinstance(value, datetime):\n                value = value.date()\n            return value\n    return DateConverter(formatter)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReturns a callable instance that will convert a string to a Date.\n\n    :param formatter: String that represents data format for parsing.\n    :return: instance of the DateConverter.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `to_date_field` takes formatter. Returns `DateConverter`. Converts strings and datetimes to dates. Uses formatter in conversion.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::73", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef callgraph(G, stmt_list):\n    func_list = []\n    for stmt in stmt_list:\n        try:\n            G.add_node(stmt.head.ident.name)\n            func_list.append(stmt)\n        except:\n            pass\n    for func in func_list:\n        assert isinstance(func, node.function)\n        func_name = func.head.ident.name\n        for s in node.postorder(func):\n            if s.__class__ is node.funcall and s.func_expr.__class__ is node.ident:\n                G.add_edge(func_name, s.func_expr.name)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nBuild callgraph of func_list, ignoring\n    built-in functions\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `callgraph` takes graph `G` and list of statements `stmt_list`. Adds nodes for functions found. For each function, adds edges showing calls made.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
