{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::76", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef remove_permissions(self, value, role='any'):\n    permission_list = self.client.list_permissions(self.id)\n    key = 'emailAddress' if '@' in value else 'domain'\n    filtered_id_list = [p['id'] for p in permission_list if p[key] == value and (p['role'] == role or role == 'any')]\n    for permission_id in filtered_id_list:\n        self.client.remove_permission(self.id, permission_id)\n    return filtered_id_list\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nRemove permissions from a user or domain.\n\n        :param value: User or domain to remove permissions from\n        :type value: str\n        :param role: (optional) Permission to remove. Defaults to all\n                     permissions.\n        :type role: str\n\n        Example::\n\n            # Remove Otto's write permission for this spreadsheet\n            sh.remove_permissions('otto@example.com', role='writer')\n\n            # Remove all Otto's permissions for this spreadsheet\n            sh.remove_permissions('otto@example.com')\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nList permissions. Filter by email or domain. Remove matching permissions. Return removed IDs.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::77", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _get_horoscope(self, day='today'):\n    if not is_valid_day(day):\n        raise HoroscopeException('Invalid day. Allowed days: [today|yesterday|tomorrow]')\n    horoscope = ''.join([str(s).strip() for s in self.tree.xpath('//*[@id=\"%s\"]/p/text()' % day)])\n    if day is 'yesterday':\n        date = self.date_today - timedelta(days=1)\n    elif day is 'today':\n        date = self.date_today\n    elif day is 'tomorrow':\n        date = self.date_today + timedelta(days=1)\n    return {'date': date.strftime('%Y-%m-%d'), 'sunsign': self.sunsign.capitalize(), 'horoscope': horoscope + '(c) Kelli Fox, The Astrologer, http://new.theastrologer.com', 'meta': self._get_horoscope_meta(day), 'credit': '(c) Kelli Fox, The Astrologer, http://new.theastrologer.com'}\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\ngets a horoscope from site html\n\n        :param day: day for which to get horoscope. Default is 'today'\n\n        :returns: dictionary of horoscope details\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction get horoscope for day. Validate day. Fetch horoscope text. Adjust date based on day. Return date, sunsign, horoscope, meta, credit.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::78", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef parse_url(url, warning=True):\n    parsed = urllib_parse.urlparse(url)\n    query = urllib_parse.parse_qs(parsed.query)\n    is_gdrive = parsed.hostname == 'drive.google.com'\n    is_download_link = parsed.path.endswith('/uc')\n    file_id = None\n    if is_gdrive and 'id' in query:\n        file_ids = query['id']\n        if len(file_ids) == 1:\n            file_id = file_ids[0]\n    match = re.match('^/file/d/(.*?)/view$', parsed.path)\n    if match:\n        file_id = match.groups()[0]\n    if is_gdrive and (not is_download_link):\n        warnings.warn('You specified Google Drive Link but it is not the correct link to download the file. Maybe you should try: {url}'.format(url='https://drive.google.com/uc?id={}'.format(file_id)))\n    return (file_id, is_download_link)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nParse URLs especially for Google Drive links.\n\n    file_id: ID of file on Google Drive.\n    is_download_link: Flag if it is download link of Google Drive.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nParse URL. Extract info. Check type. Warn if wrong. Return ID, type.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::79", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef sort_snps(snps):\n    sorted_list = sorted(snps['chrom'].unique(), key=_natural_sort_key)\n    if 'PAR' in sorted_list:\n        sorted_list.remove('PAR')\n        sorted_list.append('PAR')\n    if 'MT' in sorted_list:\n        sorted_list.remove('MT')\n        sorted_list.append('MT')\n    snps['chrom'] = snps['chrom'].astype(CategoricalDtype(categories=sorted_list, ordered=True))\n    snps = snps.sort_values(['chrom', 'pos'])\n    snps['chrom'] = snps['chrom'].astype(object)\n    return snps\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nSort SNPs based on ordered chromosome list and position.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nSort SNPs by chrom. Remove PAR and MT. Reorder categories. Sort values. Convert back. Return sorted SNPs.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::80", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef verification_digit(numbers):\n    a = sum(numbers[::2])\n    b = a * 3\n    c = sum(numbers[1::2])\n    d = b + c\n    e = d % 10\n    if e == 0:\n        return e\n    return 10 - e\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReturns the verification digit for a given numbre.\n\n        The verification digit is calculated as follows:\n\n        * A = sum of all even-positioned numbers\n        * B = A * 3\n        * C = sum of all odd-positioned numbers\n        * D = B + C\n        * The results is the smallset number N, such that (D + N) % 10 == 0\n\n        NOTE: Afip's documentation seems to have odd an even mixed up in the\n        explanation, but all examples follow the above algorithm.\n\n        :param list(int) numbers): The numbers for which the digits is to be\n            calculated.\n        :return: int\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nSum even-indexed numbers. Multiply by three. Sum odd-indexed numbers. Add both sums. Modulo ten result. If zero, return zero. Else, subtract from ten. Return final digit.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::81", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef as_dict(self):\n    out = {}\n    for prop in self:\n        propval = getattr(self, prop)\n        if hasattr(propval, 'for_json'):\n            out[prop] = propval.for_json()\n        elif isinstance(propval, list):\n            out[prop] = [getattr(x, 'for_json', lambda : x)() for x in propval]\n        elif isinstance(propval, (ProtocolBase, LiteralValue)):\n            out[prop] = propval.as_dict()\n        elif propval is not None:\n            out[prop] = propval\n    return out\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReturn a dictionary containing the current values\n        of the object.\n\n        Returns:\n            (dict): The object represented as a dictionary\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `as_dict` converts object properties to dictionary. Iterates over object props. Gets value of each prop. Checks if value has `for_json` method. If yes, calls it. If value is list, iterates over items. Calls `for_json` if exists, else uses item directly. If value is ProtocolBase or LiteralValue, calls `as_dict`. Otherwise, adds value directly. Returns resulting dictionary.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
