{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::84", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef find_focusable(node):\n    if not node.children:\n        return node\n    if node.focus:\n        return find_focusable(node.children_dict[node.focus[0]])\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nSearch for the first focusable window within the node tree\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks if node has children. If not, returns node. If focus exists, finds and returns child matching focus.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::85", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _map_smtp_headers_to_api_parameters(self, email_message):\n    api_data = []\n    for (smtp_key, api_transformer) in six.iteritems(self._headers_map):\n        data_to_transform = email_message.extra_headers.pop(smtp_key, None)\n        if data_to_transform is not None:\n            if isinstance(data_to_transform, (list, tuple)):\n                for data in data_to_transform:\n                    api_data.append((api_transformer[0], api_transformer[1](data)))\n            elif isinstance(data_to_transform, dict):\n                for data in six.iteritems(data_to_transform):\n                    api_data.append(api_transformer(data))\n            else:\n                api_data.append((api_transformer[0], api_transformer[1](data_to_transform)))\n    return api_data\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nMap the values passed in SMTP headers to API-ready\n        2-item tuples present in HEADERS_MAP\n\n        header values must be a single string or list or tuple of strings\n\n        :return: 2-item tuples of the form (api_name, api_values)\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction maps SMTP headers to API parameters. Iterates over header map. Pops headers from message. Transforms data using transformers. Appends transformed data to list. Returns list of API parameters.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::86", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _get_client(self):\n    client_kwargs = self._storage_parameters.get('client', dict())\n    if self._unsecure:\n        client_kwargs = client_kwargs.copy()\n        client_kwargs['use_ssl'] = False\n    return self._get_session().client('s3', **client_kwargs)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nS3 Boto3 client\n\n        Returns:\n            boto3.session.Session.client: client\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nGet client from storage params. If unsecure, set SSL false. Return session client with S3 and kwargs.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::87", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef save_key_file(self):\n    if self.client_key is None:\n        return\n    if self.key_file_path:\n        key_file_path = self.key_file_path\n    else:\n        key_file_path = self._get_key_file_path()\n    logger.debug('save keyfile to %s', key_file_path)\n    with open(key_file_path, 'w+') as f:\n        raw_data = f.read()\n        key_dict = {}\n        if raw_data:\n            key_dict = json.loads(raw_data)\n        key_dict[self.ip] = self.client_key\n        f.write(json.dumps(key_dict))\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nSave the current client key.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks if client key exists. If not, stop. If path given, use it; otherwise, get default path. Log saving action. Open file in write mode. Read existing data. Convert to dictionary. Add IP and client key. Write updated dictionary back to file.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
