{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::104", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_cas(key_options, global_options, item):\n    if item:\n        ign_cas = get_option('ignore_cas', key_options, globals(), False)\n        return 0 if ign_cas else item.cas\n    else:\n        try:\n            cas = key_options['cas']\n        except KeyError:\n            try:\n                cas = global_options['cas']\n            except KeyError:\n                return 0\n        if not cas:\n            return 0\n        return cas\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nGet the CAS from various inputs. This will properly honor\n    the ``ignore_cas`` flag, if present.\n\n    :param key_options: Key specific options\n    :param global_options: Global options\n    :param item: The item\n    :return: The cas, or 0 if no cas\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks if item exists. If yes, gets ignore CAS option. Returns 0 if true, else returns item's CAS value. If item doesn't exist, tries getting CAS from key options. If not found there, tries global options. If still not found, returns 0. If CAS is found but empty, also returns 0. Otherwise, returns CAS value.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::105", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef reset(self, fid=0):\n    self._checkid(fid)\n    self._fitids[fid]['solved'] = False\n    self._fitids[fid]['haserr'] = False\n    if not self._fitids[fid]['looped']:\n        return self._fitproxy.reset(fid)\n    else:\n        self._fitids[fid]['looped'] = False\n    return True\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReset the object's resources to its initialized state.\n\n        :param fid: the id of a sub-fitter\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks ID. Marks solved and haserr false. If not looped, resets proxy. Else, marks looped false. Returns true.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::106", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef parse(cls, requester, entry):\n    if not type(entry) is dict:\n        return entry\n    for (key_to_parse, cls_to_parse) in six.iteritems(cls.parser):\n        if key_to_parse in entry:\n            entry[key_to_parse] = cls_to_parse.parse(requester, entry[key_to_parse])\n    return cls(requester, **entry)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nTurns a JSON object into a model instance.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks if entry is dict. If not, returns it. Loops through parser keys. If key exists, parses value using corresponding class. Returns new instance of class with parsed values.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "conceptor_prompt::107", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _encode_filename_header(self, filename):\n    user_agent = self.request.META.get('HTTP_USER_AGENT', None)\n    if 'WebKit' in user_agent:\n        return u'filename={}'.format(filename).encode('utf-8')\n    elif 'MSIE' in user_agent:\n        url_encoded = quote(filename.encode('utf-8')).replace('attachment', 'a%74tachment')\n        return 'filename={}'.format(url_encoded).encode('utf-8')\n    else:\n        rfc2231_filename = quote(filename.encode('utf-8'))\n        return \"filename*=UTF-8''{}\".format(rfc2231_filename).encode('utf-8')\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nThe filename, encoded to use in a ``Content-Disposition`` header.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction get user agent. Check if WebKit. Encode filename. Return encoded string. If MSIE. URL encode filename. Replace attachment. Return encoded string. Else. RFC 2231 encode filename. Return encoded string.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
