{"custom_id": "proper_prompt::64", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef parse_devicelist(data_str):\n    p = HTMLTableParser()\n    p.feed(data_str)\n    known_devices = p.tables[9]\n    devices = {}\n    for device in known_devices:\n        if len(device) == 5 and device[2] != '':\n            devices[device[2]] = device[1]\n    return devices\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nParse the BT Home Hub 5 data format.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nHTML parser reads data. Extracts table at index nine. Iterates over rows. Checks length five and non-empty third column. Adds to dictionary with key second column, value third. Returns dictionary of devices.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "proper_prompt::65", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef filter_publication(publication, cache=_CACHE):\n    if cache is None:\n        cache = load_cache()\n    if publication._get_hash() in cache:\n        return None\n    cache.update([publication._get_hash()])\n    save_cache(cache)\n    return publication\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nDeduplication function, which compares `publication` with samples stored in\n    `cache`. If the match NOT is found, `publication` is returned, else None.\n\n    Args:\n        publication (obj): :class:`.Publication` instance.\n        cache (obj): Cache which is used for lookups.\n\n    Returns:\n        obj/None: Depends whether the object is found in cache or not.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks if publication hash in cache. If yes, returns none. Updates cache with hash. Saves updated cache. Returns publication.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "proper_prompt::66", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _parse(self, stream, context, path):\n    objs = []\n    while True:\n        start = stream.tell()\n        test = stream.read(len(self.find))\n        stream.seek(start)\n        if test == self.find:\n            break\n        else:\n            subobj = self.subcon._parse(stream, context, path)\n            objs.append(subobj)\n    return objs\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nParse until a given byte string is found.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nReads data from `stream`. Searches for `self.find`. If found, stops. Else, parses sub-objects and adds to list. Returns list of objects.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "proper_prompt::67", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_photometry(self, brightest=False, min_unc=0.02, convert=True):\n    if brightest:\n        row = self.brightest\n    else:\n        row = self.closest\n    if not hasattr(self, 'conversions'):\n        convert = False\n    if convert:\n        bands = self.conversions\n    else:\n        bands = self.bands.keys()\n    d = {}\n    for b in bands:\n        if convert:\n            key = b\n            (mag, dmag) = getattr(self, b)(brightest=brightest)\n        else:\n            key = self.bands[b]\n            (mag, dmag) = (row[b], row['e_{}'.format(b)])\n        d[key] = (mag, max(dmag, min_unc))\n    return d\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReturns dictionary of photometry of closest match\n\n        unless brightest is True, in which case the brightest match.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `get_photometry` fetches photometric data. If `brightest`, uses brightest star; otherwise, closest one. Checks if conversions needed. Iterates over bands, converting magnitudes if required. Stores results in dictionary with keys and values. Returns dictionary of magnitudes and uncertainties.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "proper_prompt::68", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _get_request_fields_from_parent(self):\n    if not self.parent:\n        return None\n    if not getattr(self.parent, 'request_fields'):\n        return None\n    if not isinstance(self.parent.request_fields, dict):\n        return None\n    return self.parent.request_fields.get(self.field_name)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nGet request fields from the parent serializer.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks parent exists. Parent has request fields? Check type. Return field value.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
