{"custom_id": "proper_prompt::71", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_cached_token(self):\n    token_info = None\n    if self.cache_path:\n        try:\n            f = open(self.cache_path)\n            token_info_string = f.read()\n            f.close()\n            token_info = json.loads(token_info_string)\n            if self.is_token_expired(token_info):\n                token_info = self.refresh_access_token(token_info['refresh_token'])\n        except IOError:\n            pass\n    return token_info\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nGets a cached auth token\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction reads cached token from file. If file exists and token is expired, refreshes it. Returns token info.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "proper_prompt::72", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef to_date_field(formatter):\n\n    class DateConverter(object):\n\n        def __init__(self, formatter):\n            self.formatter = formatter\n\n        def __call__(self, value):\n            if isinstance(value, string_types):\n                value = datetime.strptime(value, self.formatter).date()\n            if isinstance(value, datetime):\n                value = value.date()\n            return value\n    return DateConverter(formatter)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReturns a callable instance that will convert a string to a Date.\n\n    :param formatter: String that represents data format for parsing.\n    :return: instance of the DateConverter.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `to_date_field` takes formatter. Returns `DateConverter` class. This class converts values to dates using given formatter. If value is string, parses it with formatter. If already datetime, extracts date part. Returns converted value. Use this to standardize date inputs. Next step: create instance of `DateConverter` with specific formatter.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "proper_prompt::73", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef callgraph(G, stmt_list):\n    func_list = []\n    for stmt in stmt_list:\n        try:\n            G.add_node(stmt.head.ident.name)\n            func_list.append(stmt)\n        except:\n            pass\n    for func in func_list:\n        assert isinstance(func, node.function)\n        func_name = func.head.ident.name\n        for s in node.postorder(func):\n            if s.__class__ is node.funcall and s.func_expr.__class__ is node.ident:\n                G.add_edge(func_name, s.func_expr.name)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nBuild callgraph of func_list, ignoring\n    built-in functions\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `callgraph` takes graph `G` and list of statements `stmt_list`. Adds nodes for each statement's head identifier name. Collects these statements into `func_list`. For each function in `func_list`, asserts it's a function node. Then iterates over postorder traversal of function, adding edges from function name to called function names.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
