{"custom_id": "const_prompt::106", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef parse(cls, requester, entry):\n    if not type(entry) is dict:\n        return entry\n    for (key_to_parse, cls_to_parse) in six.iteritems(cls.parser):\n        if key_to_parse in entry:\n            entry[key_to_parse] = cls_to_parse.parse(requester, entry[key_to_parse])\n    return cls(requester, **entry)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nTurns a JSON object into a model instance.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nParse entry into dict. If not dict, return entry. For each parser key-value pair, if key in entry, parse value. Return new class instance with parsed data.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "const_prompt::107", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _encode_filename_header(self, filename):\n    user_agent = self.request.META.get('HTTP_USER_AGENT', None)\n    if 'WebKit' in user_agent:\n        return u'filename={}'.format(filename).encode('utf-8')\n    elif 'MSIE' in user_agent:\n        url_encoded = quote(filename.encode('utf-8')).replace('attachment', 'a%74tachment')\n        return 'filename={}'.format(url_encoded).encode('utf-8')\n    else:\n        rfc2231_filename = quote(filename.encode('utf-8'))\n        return \"filename*=UTF-8''{}\".format(rfc2231_filename).encode('utf-8')\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nThe filename, encoded to use in a ``Content-Disposition`` header.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nUser agent checks [detects browser type]. If WebKit, encodes filename directly. If MSIE, URL encodes then tweaks attachment. Else, RFC 2231 encodes. Returns encoded string.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
