{"custom_id": "mg_gradient_trained_probe_mse_prompt::162", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef initial_step(self, phase, x, y):\n    self.x[0] = x\n    self.y[0] = y\n    self.phase[0] = phase\n    if self.MODE == CordicMode.ROTATION:\n        if phase > 0.5:\n            self.x[0] = -x\n            self.phase[0] = phase - 1.0\n        elif phase < -0.5:\n            self.x[0] = -x\n            self.phase[0] = phase + 1.0\n    elif self.MODE == CordicMode.VECTORING:\n        if x < 0.0 and y > 0.0:\n            self.x[0] = -x\n            self.y[0] = -y\n            self.phase[0] = 1.0\n        elif x < 0.0 and y < 0.0:\n            self.x[0] = -x\n            self.y[0] = -y\n            self.phase[0] = -1.0\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nTransform input to the CORDIC working quadrants\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `initial_step` sets initial values for `x`, `y`, and `phase`. Adjusts based on `MODE` and `phase` value. If in rotation mode, flips `x` and adjusts `phase`. If in vectoring mode, flips `x` and `y` based on quadrant, setting `phase`. Next step is processing based on adjusted values.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "mg_gradient_trained_probe_mse_prompt::163", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef dispatch_queue(loader):\n    queue = loader._queue\n    loader._queue = []\n    max_batch_size = loader.max_batch_size\n    if max_batch_size and max_batch_size < len(queue):\n        chunks = get_chunks(queue, max_batch_size)\n        for chunk in chunks:\n            dispatch_queue_batch(loader, chunk)\n    else:\n        dispatch_queue_batch(loader, queue)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nGiven the current state of a Loader instance, perform a batch load\n    from its current queue.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nLoader clear queue. Empty queue now. Check max batch size. If set and less than queue length, split queue into chunks. Dispatch each chunk. Else, dispatch whole queue.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
