{"custom_id": "mg_gradient_trained_probe_nll_alone::115", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_historical_minute_data(self, ticker: str):\n    start = self._start\n    stop = self._stop\n    if len(stop) > 4:\n        stop = stop[:4]\n    if len(start) > 4:\n        start = start[:4]\n    for year in range(int(start), int(stop) + 1):\n        beg_time = '%s0101000000' % year\n        end_time = '%s1231235959' % year\n        msg = 'HIT,%s,60,%s,%s,,,,1,,,s\\r\\n' % (ticker, beg_time, end_time)\n        try:\n            data = iq.iq_query(message=msg)\n            iq.add_data_to_df(data=data)\n        except Exception as err:\n            log.error('No data returned because %s', err)\n    try:\n        self.dfdb.write_points(self._ndf, ticker)\n    except InfluxDBClientError as err:\n        log.error('Write to database failed: %s' % err)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nRequest historical 5 minute data from DTN.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nThe function `get_historical_minute_data` fetches historical minute-level stock data for a specified ticker over a given time period. It iterates through each year from the start date to the end date, constructs a message requesting data for that year, sends it using `iq.iq_query`, and adds the received data to a DataFrame. If any error occurs during this process, it logs an error message. After collecting all data, it attempts to write the DataFrame to an InfluxDB database. If writing fails, another error message is logged. This ensures that all available data is processed and stored correctly.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or onl