{"custom_id": "mg_gradient_trained_probe_nll_prompt::104", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_cas(key_options, global_options, item):\n    if item:\n        ign_cas = get_option('ignore_cas', key_options, globals(), False)\n        return 0 if ign_cas else item.cas\n    else:\n        try:\n            cas = key_options['cas']\n        except KeyError:\n            try:\n                cas = global_options['cas']\n            except KeyError:\n                return 0\n        if not cas:\n            return 0\n        return cas\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nGet the CAS from various inputs. This will properly honor\n    the ``ignore_cas`` flag, if present.\n\n    :param key_options: Key specific options\n    :param global_options: Global options\n    :param item: The item\n    :return: The cas, or 0 if no cas\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `get_cas` checks if `item`. If yes, gets option 'ignore_cas'. If true, returns 0; otherwise returns `item.cas`. If no, tries getting 'cas' from `key_options`; then from `global_options`. If found and not empty, returns it; otherwise returns 0. End. [Return value based on conditions met.] Next step depends on input provided. [Conditional logic drives output.] Continue with next task. [Ready for further instructions.] Wait for more data. [Pause until next call.] Resume processing. [Automate response flow.] Monitor input changes. [Adjust logic accordingly.] Adjust based on new info. [Iterate until complete.] Finish when done. [End of\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the