{"custom_id": "mg_gradient_trained_probe_nll_prompt::105", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef reset(self, fid=0):\n    self._checkid(fid)\n    self._fitids[fid]['solved'] = False\n    self._fitids[fid]['haserr'] = False\n    if not self._fitids[fid]['looped']:\n        return self._fitproxy.reset(fid)\n    else:\n        self._fitids[fid]['looped'] = False\n    return True\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReset the object's resources to its initialized state.\n\n        :param fid: the id of a sub-fitter\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `reset` checks ID, resets solved and error flags, unloops if needed, then calls proxy reset. Returns true. Next step? Continue with next task. [End]\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "mg_gradient_trained_probe_nll_prompt::106", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef parse(cls, requester, entry):\n    if not type(entry) is dict:\n        return entry\n    for (key_to_parse, cls_to_parse) in six.iteritems(cls.parser):\n        if key_to_parse in entry:\n            entry[key_to_parse] = cls_to_parse.parse(requester, entry[key_to_parse])\n    return cls(requester, **entry)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nTurns a JSON object into a model instance.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `parse` checks if input is dictionary. If yes, it loops over parser's keys and classes. For each matching key, it calls corresponding class's parse method with current value and requester. Then it creates new instance of class using parsed values. Returns this new instance. If input isn't dictionary, returns it unchanged. Continue with next command. [End]\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "mg_gradient_trained_probe_nll_prompt::107", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _encode_filename_header(self, filename):\n    user_agent = self.request.META.get('HTTP_USER_AGENT', None)\n    if 'WebKit' in user_agent:\n        return u'filename={}'.format(filename).encode('utf-8')\n    elif 'MSIE' in user_agent:\n        url_encoded = quote(filename.encode('utf-8')).replace('attachment', 'a%74tachment')\n        return 'filename={}'.format(url_encoded).encode('utf-8')\n    else:\n        rfc2231_filename = quote(filename.encode('utf-8'))\n        return \"filename*=UTF-8''{}\".format(rfc2231_filename).encode('utf-8')\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nThe filename, encoded to use in a ``Content-Disposition`` header.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks user agent. If WebKit, encodes filename directly. If MSIE, URL-encodes and tweaks string. Else, uses RFC 2231 encoding. Returns encoded filename header. Next step? Use returned value in response. Continue. [End]\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
