{"custom_id": "mg_dim_probe_nll_prompt::12", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef convert_coordinates(coords, origin, wgs84, wrapped):\n    if isinstance(coords, list) or isinstance(coords, tuple):\n        try:\n            if isinstance(coords[0], list) or isinstance(coords[0], tuple):\n                return [convert_coordinates(list(c), origin, wgs84, wrapped) for c in coords]\n            elif isinstance(coords[0], float):\n                c = list(transform(origin, wgs84, *coords))\n                if wrapped and c[0] < -170:\n                    c[0] = c[0] + 360\n                return c\n        except IndexError:\n            pass\n    return None\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nConvert coordinates from one crs to another\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks if input is list or tuple. If so, recursively processes each element. Converts coordinates using `transform` function from `origin` to `wgs84`. Adjusts longitude if wrapped and less than -170 degrees. Returns transformed coordinates or None.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
