{"custom_id": "mg_dim_probe_nll_prompt::55", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef run(self, host, port=25, with_ssl=False):\n    try:\n        dns_rec = self._lookup(host, port)\n        self._connect(dns_rec)\n        if with_ssl:\n            self._wrap_ssl()\n        banner = self._get_banner()\n        self._check_banner(banner)\n    except Exception:\n        (exc_type, exc_value, exc_tb) = sys.exc_info()\n        self.results['Exception-Type'] = str(exc_type.__name__)\n        self.results['Exception-Value'] = str(exc_value)\n        self.results['Exception-Traceback'] = repr(traceback.format_exc())\n    finally:\n        self._close(with_ssl)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nExecutes a single health check against a remote host and port. This\n        method may only be called once per object.\n\n        :param host: The hostname or IP address of the SMTP server to check.\n        :type host: str\n        :param port: The port number of the SMTP server to check.\n        :type port: int\n        :param with_ssl: If ``True``, SSL will be initiated before attempting\n                         to get the banner message.\n        :type with_ssl: bool\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `run` starts. Takes `host`, optional `port`, and `with_ssl`. Tries DNS lookup. Connects. If SSL, wraps. Gets banner. Checks banner. Catches exceptions. Logs type, value, traceback. Finally closes connection.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "mg_dim_probe_nll_prompt::56", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef add_pass_thru(pass_thrus):\n\n    def meth(self, node):\n        pass\n\n    def dec(cls):\n        for element_name in pass_thrus:\n            for meth_prefix in ('visit_', 'depart_'):\n                meth_name = meth_prefix + element_name\n                if hasattr(cls, meth_name):\n                    raise ValueError('method name {} already defined'.format(meth_name))\n                setattr(cls, meth_name, meth)\n        return cls\n    return dec\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nDecorator adds explicit pass-through visit and depart methods\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `add_pass_thru` takes list of elements and returns decorator. Decorator adds methods named `visit_<element>` and `depart_<element>` to class, if they don't exist. If method exists, raises error.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
