{"custom_id": "mg_dim_probe_nll_prompt::65", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef filter_publication(publication, cache=_CACHE):\n    if cache is None:\n        cache = load_cache()\n    if publication._get_hash() in cache:\n        return None\n    cache.update([publication._get_hash()])\n    save_cache(cache)\n    return publication\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nDeduplication function, which compares `publication` with samples stored in\n    `cache`. If the match NOT is found, `publication` is returned, else None.\n\n    Args:\n        publication (obj): :class:`.Publication` instance.\n        cache (obj): Cache which is used for lookups.\n\n    Returns:\n        obj/None: Depends whether the object is found in cache or not.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks pub hash in cache. If found, returns none. Else updates cache and saves it. Returns pub.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "mg_dim_probe_nll_prompt::66", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _parse(self, stream, context, path):\n    objs = []\n    while True:\n        start = stream.tell()\n        test = stream.read(len(self.find))\n        stream.seek(start)\n        if test == self.find:\n            break\n        else:\n            subobj = self.subcon._parse(stream, context, path)\n            objs.append(subobj)\n    return objs\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nParse until a given byte string is found.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nReads stream until finds specific marker. Parses each chunk into objects. Returns list of parsed objects.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "mg_dim_probe_nll_prompt::67", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_photometry(self, brightest=False, min_unc=0.02, convert=True):\n    if brightest:\n        row = self.brightest\n    else:\n        row = self.closest\n    if not hasattr(self, 'conversions'):\n        convert = False\n    if convert:\n        bands = self.conversions\n    else:\n        bands = self.bands.keys()\n    d = {}\n    for b in bands:\n        if convert:\n            key = b\n            (mag, dmag) = getattr(self, b)(brightest=brightest)\n        else:\n            key = self.bands[b]\n            (mag, dmag) = (row[b], row['e_{}'.format(b)])\n        d[key] = (mag, max(dmag, min_unc))\n    return d\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReturns dictionary of photometry of closest match\n\n        unless brightest is True, in which case the brightest match.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction fetches photometry data. Filters by brightest star or closest object. Adjusts for conversions if needed. Returns magnitudes and uncertainties.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "mg_dim_probe_nll_prompt::68", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _get_request_fields_from_parent(self):\n    if not self.parent:\n        return None\n    if not getattr(self.parent, 'request_fields'):\n        return None\n    if not isinstance(self.parent.request_fields, dict):\n        return None\n    return self.parent.request_fields.get(self.field_name)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nGet request fields from the parent serializer.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks parent exists. Parent has request fields? Check type. Get field value. Return it.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
