{"custom_id": "mg_dim_probe_nll_prompt::92", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef valuedispatch(func):\n    registry = {}\n\n    def dispatch(value):\n        return registry.get(value, func)\n\n    def register(value, func=None):\n        if func is None:\n            return lambda f: register(value, f)\n        registry[value] = func\n        return func\n\n    def wrapper(*args, **kw):\n        return dispatch(args[0])(*args, **kw)\n    wrapper.register = register\n    wrapper.dispatch = dispatch\n    wrapper.registry = MappingProxyType(registry)\n    update_wrapper(wrapper, func)\n    return wrapper\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nDecorates a function to dispatch handler of the value of the first\n    argument.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `valuedispatch` takes another function and returns a wrapper. Wrapper has methods to register values with functions, dispatch calls based on value, and access registry.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "mg_dim_probe_nll_prompt::93", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef create_service_from_endpoint(endpoint, service_type, title=None, abstract=None, catalog=None):\n    from models import Service\n    if Service.objects.filter(url=endpoint, catalog=catalog).count() == 0:\n        request = requests.get(endpoint)\n        if request.status_code == 200:\n            LOGGER.debug('Creating a %s service for endpoint=%s catalog=%s' % (service_type, endpoint, catalog))\n            service = Service(type=service_type, url=endpoint, title=title, abstract=abstract, csw_type='service', catalog=catalog)\n            service.save()\n            return service\n        else:\n            LOGGER.warning('This endpoint is invalid, status code is %s' % request.status_code)\n    else:\n        LOGGER.warning('A service for this endpoint %s in catalog %s already exists' % (endpoint, catalog))\n        return None\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nCreate a service from an endpoint if it does not already exists.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction checks if service exists. If not, fetches data. Creates and saves service if valid. Logs actions accordingly. Returns service or `None`.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "mg_dim_probe_nll_prompt::94", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef on_init(app):\n    docs_path = os.path.abspath(os.path.dirname(__file__))\n    root_path = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(docs_path, '..'))\n    apidoc_path = 'sphinx-apidoc'\n    swg2rst_path = 'swg2rst'\n    if hasattr(sys, 'real_prefix'):\n        bin_path = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(sys.prefix, 'bin'))\n        apidoc_path = os.path.join(bin_path, apidoc_path)\n        swg2rst_path = os.path.join(bin_path, swg2rst_path)\n    check_call([apidoc_path, '-o', docs_path, os.path.join(root_path, 'user_tasks'), os.path.join(root_path, 'user_tasks/migrations')])\n    json_path = os.path.join(docs_path, 'swagger.json')\n    rst_path = os.path.join(docs_path, 'rest_api.rst')\n    check_call([swg2rst_path, json_path, '-f', 'rst', '-o', rst_path])\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nRun sphinx-apidoc and swg2rst after Sphinx initialization.\n\n    Read the Docs won't run tox or custom shell commands, so we need this to\n    avoid checking in the generated reStructuredText files.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `on_init` sets paths for documentation and tools. Checks if in virtual environment adjusts paths accordingly. Runs `sphinx-apidoc` to generate API docs. Converts Swagger JSON to RST format.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
