{"custom_id": "mg_dim_probe_nll_prompt::144", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef serialize(data, format: str='json', pretty: bool=False):\n\n    def encode(obj):\n        if isinstance(obj, stellata.model.Model):\n            return obj.to_dict()\n        elif isinstance(obj, datetime.datetime):\n            return int(obj.timestamp())\n        elif isinstance(obj, datetime.date):\n            return obj.isoformat()\n        elif isinstance(obj, decimal.Decimal):\n            return float(obj)\n        elif hasattr(obj, 'serialize'):\n            return obj.serialize()\n        return obj\n    if format == 'msgpack':\n        return msgpack.packb(data, default=encode)\n    if format == 'json':\n        if pretty:\n            return json.dumps(data, default=encode, indent=4)\n        return json.dumps(data, default=encode)\n    return data\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nSerialize a stellata object to a string format.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `serialize` takes data, format type, and pretty print option. Encodes objects using helper function `encode`. Formats output as JSON or MessagePack based on input. Pretty prints JSON if requested. Returns serialized data.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent