{"custom_id": "mg_conc_probe_mse_prompt::66", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _parse(self, stream, context, path):\n    objs = []\n    while True:\n        start = stream.tell()\n        test = stream.read(len(self.find))\n        stream.seek(start)\n        if test == self.find:\n            break\n        else:\n            subobj = self.subcon._parse(stream, context, path)\n            objs.append(subobj)\n    return objs\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nParse until a given byte string is found.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nReads stream until finds specific bytes. Parses each found object. Collects objects in list. Returns list of parsed objects.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "mg_conc_probe_mse_prompt::67", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef get_photometry(self, brightest=False, min_unc=0.02, convert=True):\n    if brightest:\n        row = self.brightest\n    else:\n        row = self.closest\n    if not hasattr(self, 'conversions'):\n        convert = False\n    if convert:\n        bands = self.conversions\n    else:\n        bands = self.bands.keys()\n    d = {}\n    for b in bands:\n        if convert:\n            key = b\n            (mag, dmag) = getattr(self, b)(brightest=brightest)\n        else:\n            key = self.bands[b]\n            (mag, dmag) = (row[b], row['e_{}'.format(b)])\n        d[key] = (mag, max(dmag, min_unc))\n    return d\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nReturns dictionary of photometry of closest match\n\n        unless brightest is True, in which case the brightest match.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction fetches photometry data. Checks if brightest star needed. Sets row accordingly. Converts magnitudes if possible. Iterates over bands, fetching magnitudes and uncertainties. Ensures minimum uncertainty applied. Returns dictionary of magnitudes and uncertainties.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
{"custom_id": "mg_conc_probe_mse_prompt::68", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _get_request_fields_from_parent(self):\n    if not self.parent:\n        return None\n    if not getattr(self.parent, 'request_fields'):\n        return None\n    if not isinstance(self.parent.request_fields, dict):\n        return None\n    return self.parent.request_fields.get(self.field_name)\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nGet request fields from the parent serializer.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction check parent exists. Check parent has request fields. Check request fields is dictionary. Get field value from parent. Return value or none.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
