{"custom_id": "sg_clamp_probe_nll_prompt::117", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef drape(raster, feature):\n    coords = feature['geometry']['coordinates']\n    geom_type = feature['geometry']['type']\n    if geom_type == 'Point':\n        xyz = sample(raster, [coords])\n        result = Point(xyz[0])\n    elif geom_type == 'LineString':\n        xyz = sample(raster, coords)\n        points = [Point(x, y, z) for (x, y, z) in xyz]\n        result = LineString(points)\n    else:\n        logging.error('drape not implemented for {}'.format(geom_type))\n    return result\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nConvert a 2D feature to a 3D feature by sampling a raster\n\n    Parameters:\n        raster (rasterio): raster to provide the z coordinate\n        feature (dict): fiona feature record to convert\n\n    Returns:\n        result (Point or Linestring): shapely Point or LineString of xyz coordinate triples\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `drape` takes raster and feature. Extracts coordinates and type from feature. If point, samples raster at coordinate. Creates point with sampled value. If line string, samples raster along coordinates. Creates line string with sampled values. For other types, logs error. Returns result.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no