{"custom_id": "sg_clamp_probe_nll_prompt::139", "method": "POST", "url": "/v1/chat/completions", "body": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are grading an automatically generated explanation of a Python function.\n\nFunction:\n```python\ndef _inner_product(y, yr, psd):\n    fmin = 40.0\n    fmax = 2000.0\n    fs = 16384.0\n    y = 1.0 / fs * y\n    yr = 1.0 / fs * yr\n    p = np.multiply(y, np.conjugate(yr)) / psd\n    product = max(abs(fs * sp.ifft(np.multiply(y, np.conjugate(yr)) / psd)))\n    return product\n```\n\nReference explanation (written by the original developer, for grading only):\nCompute inner product between two time domain waveforms, weighted by noisecurve.\n\nCandidate explanation to grade:\nFunction `_inner_product` calculates inner product of signals `y` and `yr`. Normalizes `y` and `yr` by sampling frequency `fs`. Multiplies `y` with conjugate of `yr`, divides by power spectral density `psd`. Takes maximum absolute value of inverse Fourier transform result. Returns this maximum value.\n\nScore the candidate explanation on two axes:\n- \"correct\": 0 if it is wrong or misleading about what the function does, 1 if it is vague or only partially\n  correct, 2 if it correctly captures the function's actual behavior (wording may differ from the reference).\n- \"coherent\": false if the text is degenerate, repetitive, non-English gibberish, or so garbled it fails to\n  read as a genuine explanation; true otherwise.\n\nRespond with ONLY a JSON object, no other text: {\"correct\": <0|1|2>, \"coherent\": <true|false>}"}]}}
